#. [unit_type]: id=Asa_Sergeant, gender=female
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Asa/Asa_L1.cfg:8
msgid "female^Frontier Warrior"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Asa_Sergeant, gender=female
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Asa/Asa_L1.cfg:11
msgid "Sergeants are low-ranking officers of human armies. Though academically trained, they need some experience in the field before their leadership is sound and acknowledged. Still, their diligent bearing and basic insight of combat means they can more effectively rouse civilians and peasants in trying situations."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Asa_Lieutenant, gender=female
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Asa/Asa_L2.cfg:8
msgid "female^Veteran Warrior"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Asa_Lieutenant, gender=female
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Asa/Asa_L2.cfg:11
msgid "Lieutenants are some of the more respected commanding officers among humans and are often seen leading smaller-scale incursions and managing the battlefield. Trained both with sword and crossbow, they excel at neither, and are somewhat less resilient than the warlords of other races — this is more than made up for by their superior knowledge and training in military strategy."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Asa_General, gender=female
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Asa/Asa_L3.cfg:8
msgid "female^Frontier Commander"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Asa_General, gender=female
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Asa/Asa_L3.cfg:11
msgid "As the leaders of their armies, Generals are responsible for the protection of large or important areas in the kingdoms to which they have sworn fealty. Well seasoned in the art of war, Generals can direct even the freshest recruits to strike strategically against imposing odds and emerge victorious. Recognized by nobility and citizenry alike, they are outfitted in ornate plate armor and granted some of the finest weaponry that human craftsmen can offer."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Asa_Grand_Marshal, gender=female
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Asa/Asa_L4.cfg:8
msgid "female^Veteran Commander"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Asa_Grand_Marshal, gender=female
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Asa/Asa_L4.cfg:10
msgid "The rank of Grand Marshal is one of the most esteemed in the armies of humanity, and those who bear its title have survived many trials by fire, proving both their tactical wit and their considerable mettle at personal combat."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Daeola_L0, race=human, gender=female
#. [unit_type]: id=Child, race=human, gender=male,female
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Daeola/Daeola_L0.cfg:8
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Others/Child.cfg:4
msgid "Child"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Daeola_L0, race=human, gender=female
#. [unit_type]: id=Child, race=human, gender=male,female
#. Звичайна людська дитина, що ще ви очікували тут прочитати?
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Daeola/Daeola_L0.cfg:18
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Others/Child.cfg:19
msgid "An ordinary human child, what else did you expect to read here?"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Daeola_L0_Apprentice, race=human, gender=female
#. [unit_type]: id=Daeola_L0_Apprentice_Unarmed, race=human, gender=female
#. [unit_type]: id=Apprentice, race=human
#. Будь-який маг починав свій шлях як ученик, бо ж самому без допомоги більш досвідченого чаклуна практично неможливо зрозуміти сутність магії та навчитися її основ, хіба що новачок має неймовірний талант або його веде вища сила
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Daeola/Daeola_L0_Apprentice.cfg:21
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Daeola/Daeola_L0_Apprentice_Unarmed.cfg:21
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Mages/Apprentice.cfg:18
msgid "Any future mage begin their journey as an apprentice, because without the help of a more experienced sorcerer it's almost impossible to understand the essence of magic and learn its basics, unless the beginner has an incredible talent or is guided by a higher power."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Daeola_L1_Mage, race=human, gender=female
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Daeola/Daeola_L1_Mage.cfg:8
msgid "Light Mage"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Daeola_L1_Mage, race=human, gender=female
#. Ті, хто кличуться Магами Світла знаходяться на набагато більшому рівні розуміння цілительства та самого Світла, ніж Mage Healers і навіть White Mages. Вони, хоч і поки що можуть бути недостатньо мудрими, наївними чи мати мало досвіду, повністю посвятили своє життя та розум добру та допомозі нужденним, за що вони легко заслуговують повагу більшості людей Зеленого Острову.
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Daeola/Daeola_L1_Mage.cfg:23
msgid "Those who are called Light Mages are on a much higher level of understanding of healing and the Light itself than Mage Healers and even White Mages. They may yet be lacking in wisdom, naive and have little experience, but they have devoted their lives and minds to goodness and helping those in need, and for this they easily earn the respect of most of the people of the Green Isle."
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=impact
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Daeola/Daeola_L1_Mage.cfg:36
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Haralin/Haralin_L2.cfg:32
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Mages/Apprentice.cfg:24
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Mages/Mage_Healer.cfg:23
msgid "staff"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Daeola_L2, race=human, gender=female, description=
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Daeola/Daeola_L2.cfg:8
msgid "Prophetess of Light"
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=arcane
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Daeola/Daeola_L2.cfg:34
msgid "touch of light"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Haralin_L0, race=human
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Haralin/Haralin_L0.cfg:8
msgid "Young Peasant"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Haralin_L0, race=human
#. [unit_type]: id=Ruffian_Peasant
#. Селянська молодь Зеленого Острову з ранніх літ залучена до тяжкої праці на полі, випасу худоби чи навчанню професії своїх батьків. Проте, хоч і більшість свого дня вони не мають часу навіть спочити, час від часу вони збираються на сільські забави, боротьбу, а також щоб допомогти стражам села відбити напад загарбників
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Haralin/Haralin_L0.cfg:19
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Others/Villagers.cfg:48
msgid "From an early age, Green Isle's peasant youth are involved in hard labor in the fields, herding cattle, or learning their parents' craft. However, although most of their day is spent without even a moment of rest, they occasionally gather for village games, wrestling, and to help the village guards repel invaders."
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=impact
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Haralin/Haralin_L0.cfg:26
msgid "club"
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=impact
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Haralin/Haralin_L0.cfg:35
msgid "sling"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Haralin_L1, race=human, gender=male
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Haralin/Haralin_L1.cfg:8
msgid "Autodidact Mage"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Haralin_L1, race=human, gender=male
#. Це справді неймовірна рідкість, щоб звичайна людина могла самостійно осягнути суть магії та зрозуміти її основи без допомоги більш досвідченого наставника, якою б вона талановитою не була та які б ресурси не мала. Деякі кажуть, що насправді маги-самоучки не досягли всього самі, а їм допомогала якась невідома вища сила, проте це все одно вражає, чи не так?
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Haralin/Haralin_L1.cfg:22
msgid "It is indeed incredibly rare for an ordinary person to be able to understand the essence of magic and learn its basics without the help of a more experienced mentor, no matter how talented they are or what resources they have. Some people say that self-taught magicians didn't actually achieve everything on their own, but were helped by some unknown higher power, but it's still impressive anyway, isn't it?"
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=blade
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Haralin/Haralin_L1.cfg:31
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Mages/Rogue_Mage.cfg:26
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Mages/Shadow_Mage.cfg:33
msgid "short sword"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Haralin_L2, race=human, gender=male
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Haralin/Haralin_L2.cfg:8
msgid "Sorcerer"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Haralin_L2, race=human, gender=male
#. Після багатьох років старанного вивчення магії, розробки заклинань та медитацій, маг іноді може досягнути рівня, коли він вважатиметься наймогутнішим серед своїх колег з Зеленого Острову, та й навіть деякі з західняків почнуть зважати на його силу. Хоча порівняно зі здібністю більшості некромантів це досі ніщо, а про безсмертних Ліч-Лордів взагалі й згадувати нема сенсу, вони поза будь-якою конкуренцією.
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Haralin/Haralin_L2.cfg:22
msgid "After many years of hard study of magic, crafting spells and meditating, a sorcerers may sometimes reach a level where they are considered very powerful among their Green Isle colleagues, and even some Wesfolk will begin to take note of their skills. Although this is still nothing compared to the abilities of most necromancers, and there is no point in even mentioning the immortal Lich-Lords, they are beyond any competition."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Haralin_L3, race=human, gender=male
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Haralin/Haralin_L3.cfg:8
msgid "Spell Knight"
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=impact
#. [attack]: type=blade
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Haralin/Haralin_L3.cfg:31
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Mages/Arcane_Enforcer.cfg:40
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Others/Highlander.cfg:46
msgid "sword"
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=fire
#. [object]
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Mages/Apprentice.cfg:33
#: Chasing_the_Light/utils/spellcasting.cfg:30
#: Chasing_the_Light/utils/spellcasting.cfg:48
#: Chasing_the_Light/utils/spellcasting.cfg:61
msgid "missile"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Arcane Enforcer, race=human, gender=male,female
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Mages/Arcane_Enforcer.cfg:4
msgid "Arcane Enforcer"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Arcane Enforcer, race=human, gender=male,female
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Mages/Arcane_Enforcer.cfg:18
msgid "The harsh, violent life of an outlaw does not readily lend itself to magical study. Rogue mages who survive their first few years often do so with the aid of organized bandit gangs, who are more than happy to provide protection in return for muscle and loyalty. Outfitted with stolen crossbows and augmenting their piecemeal armor with scraps of half-remembered magic, these ex-magi brawl with surprising competence, especially under the cover of darkness."
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=pierce
#. [attack]: type=fire
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Mages/Arcane_Enforcer.cfg:49
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Others/Crossbowman.cfg:37
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Others/Crossbowman.cfg:49
msgid "crossbow"
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=arcane
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Mages/Arcane_Enforcer.cfg:58
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Mages/Rogue_Mage.cfg:35
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Mages/Shadow_Lord.cfg:69
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Mages/Shadow_Mage.cfg:45
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Wesfolk/Princess.cfg:72
msgid "shadow wave"
msgstr ""

#. [female]: gender=female
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Mages/Arcane_Enforcer.cfg:121
msgid "female^Arcane Enforcer"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Mage Healer, race=human
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Mages/Mage_Healer.cfg:4
msgid "Mage Healer"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Mage Healer, race=human
#. Деякі маги вирішують присвятити своє життя служінню іншим і тому основним фокусом своїх досліджень ставлять зцілення нуждених та боротьбу з істотами Темряви. Ті, що лише нещодавно стали на цей шлях, вже заслуговують називатися магами цілителями, проте їм предстоїть досягти їм ще багато, щоб стати справжніми служителями Світла
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Mages/Mage_Healer.cfg:18
msgid "Some mages choose to dedicate their lives to serving others and therefore focus their research on healing the needy and fighting the creatures of the Darkness. Those who have only recently embarked on this path already deserve to be called mage healers, but they have much to accomplish to become true servants of the Light"
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=impact
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Mages/Mage_Healer.cfg:32
msgid "magic entangle"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Rogue Mage, race=human, gender=male,female
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Mages/Rogue_Mage.cfg:5
msgid "Rogue Mage"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Rogue Mage, race=human, gender=male,female
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Mages/Rogue_Mage.cfg:19
msgid ""
"Not every student has the skill and temperment to become a mage. Novices often find themselves abandoned by their masters, sometimes for attempting to practice forbidden arts, but more often for mundane transgressions such as theft or embezzlement, or even a simple lack of funds.\n"
"\n"
"While most of these failed wizards switch to other paths, a driven few turn to banditry as a way of continuing to fund their independent studies. Now completely outside the law, Rogue Mages do whatever is necessary to support themselves, and will often dabble in the use of black magic as a result. Although they are rarely as skilled as wizards with more formal training, their spells can still be quite lethal, and their banditry has resulted in moderate skill with the short sword."
msgstr ""

#. [female]: gender=female
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Mages/Rogue_Mage.cfg:80
msgid "female^Rogue Mage"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Shadow Lord, race=human, gender=male,female
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Mages/Shadow_Lord.cfg:18
msgid "Shadow Lord"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Shadow Lord, race=human, gender=male,female
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Mages/Shadow_Lord.cfg:36
msgid "The fruits of the paths of either light or darkness are well known to magi: the brilliance of a white mage or the deep gloom of a necromancer. Much less well known is the art of the Shadow Lord, those few who master a union of both white and black magic. Though decades of zealous study and self-neglect have left them drained of strength, these savants have transcended the need for crude physical weapons, instead channeling their energies into devastating magical attacks that undercut their enemies’ resistances."
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=any
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Mages/Shadow_Lord.cfg:48
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Wesfolk/Princess.cfg:51
msgid "astral blade"
msgstr ""

#. [female]: gender=female
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Mages/Shadow_Lord.cfg:107
msgid "female^Shadow Lord"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Shadow Mage, race=human, gender=male,female
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Mages/Shadow_Mage.cfg:5
msgid "Shadow Mage"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Shadow Mage, race=human, gender=male,female
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Mages/Shadow_Mage.cfg:22
msgid "Dabbling in many schools of magic yet fully embracing none, the impoverished, obsessive study of an independent mage can sometimes yield impressive results. Unrestrained by the structure of formal apprenticeship, Shadow Magi have learned to weave together spell and sword, seizing the secrets of both light and darkness with equal fervor. When the forces of law or chaos arrive to retaliate, they cloak themselves in shadow and vanish into the night."
msgstr ""

#. [female]: gender=female
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Mages/Shadow_Mage.cfg:83
msgid "female^Shadow Mage"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Chimera, race=monster
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Monsters/Chimera.cfg:4
msgid "Chimera"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Chimera, race=monster
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Monsters/Chimera.cfg:18
msgid "Only a wicked evil wizard could have taken the characteristics of various monsters and have put them together in a single weapon of their cause. With three tails, a pair of feathery wings, the body of a gigantic bird and the eyes of a fearsome Cockatrice, this Chimera is not a foe to play with. Its ability to turn its opponents to stone is probably the major threat it imposes over its victims. Use extreme caution, and never look directly to its eyes."
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=cold
#. [attack]: type=arcane
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Monsters/Chimera.cfg:43
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Monsters/Cockatrice.cfg:35
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Monsters/Eyestalk.cfg:56
msgid "gaze"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Cockatrice, race=monster
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Monsters/Cockatrice.cfg:4
msgid "Cockatrice"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Cockatrice, race=monster
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Monsters/Cockatrice.cfg:18
msgid "Sometimes known as ‘basilisks’, these mystical creatures are said to be able to turn the living to stone. Needless to say, this makes them extremely dangerous."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Eyestalk, race=monster
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Monsters/Eyestalk.cfg:4
msgid "Eyestalk"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Eyestalk, race=monster
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Monsters/Eyestalk.cfg:25
msgid "Named ‘Eyestalks’ for obvious reasons, these plant-like creatures can focus their gaze onto an unsuspecting victim to draw life energy straight out of them to replenish their own. While almost defenseless against melee attacks, its deadly gaze from afar is not to be underestimated."
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=impact
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Monsters/Eyestalk.cfg:32
msgid "smash"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Leech, race=monster
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Monsters/Leech.cfg:4
msgid "Leech"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Leech, race=monster
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Monsters/Leech.cfg:44
msgid ""
"Leeches are universally known for their common diet, the warm blood of various bigger creatures. However, this is exactly why they are often used for medicinal purposes.\n"
"\n"
"Although not directly related, the same name is applied to groups of strange worms attached to the ground, found under caves, who are not a great danger as they cannot move around to search for prey. Instead, they await unwary victims who get close enough for them to be able to trap them in their deadly tentacles and then swallow their blood, which increases their strength and heals their wounds.\n"
"\n"
"It is fortunate that they have not developed legs; otherwise, they would be an almost unstoppable menace to explorers and dwellers of the caves they inhabit."
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=pierce
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Monsters/Leech.cfg:58
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Monsters/Leech_Brain_Drainer.cfg:31
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Monsters/Leech_Giant.cfg:29
msgid "drainer"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Brain Drainer, race=monster
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Monsters/Leech_Brain_Drainer.cfg:4
msgid "Brain Drainer"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Brain Drainer, race=monster
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Monsters/Leech_Brain_Drainer.cfg:22
msgid ""
"Giant Leeches grow up after draining enough blood, becoming a extremely dangerous threat for any living creature. As they drain blood, they regenerate, healing their wounds and growing in size.\n"
"\n"
"Since they have acquired the habit of attacking their prey’s head first, they have been named ‘brain-drainers’. This does not mean that they actually feed on their prey’s brain. They just crush its cranium with their powerful mouth in order to gain easy and fast access to the blood in the remaining body of the poor victim."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Giant Leech, race=monster
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Monsters/Leech_Giant.cfg:4
msgid "Giant Leech"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Giant Leech, race=monster
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Monsters/Leech_Giant.cfg:21
msgid ""
"Leeches are well known for their habit of draining the blood out of bigger creatures. It is fortunate that they are smaller than a man’s thumb.\n"
"\n"
"However, in certain places, deep underground, giant eyeless reptilians that behave as leeches have been spotted, thus leading people to call them ‘Giant Leeches’. It is not known what these beings actually are, or how they got to have this body structure and habits. Rumor has it that they are eternally thirsty for fresh blood."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Spider Egg, race=monster
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Monsters/Spider_Egg.cfg:4
msgid "Spiderling Egg"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Spider Egg, race=monster
#. Здоровенні огидні кокони, що десятками, якщо не сотнями, лежать в глибоких закутках печер Зламаних Гір, якийсь час ростять всередині себе неймовірно велику та огидну істоту, яка в будь-який момент готова вирватися, щоб кусати та полювати на своїх жертв.
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Monsters/Spider_Egg.cfg:67
msgid "Huge nasty cocoons, dozens if not hundreds of them, lying in the deep recesses of the Broken Mountains caves, have been nurturing an incredibly large and disgusting creatures inside them for some time, ready to break free at any moment to bite and hunt theirs victims."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Spiderling, race=monster
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Monsters/Spiderling.cfg:4
msgid "Spiderling"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Spiderling, race=monster
#. Цей здоровенний павук всього лиш дитинча, котре зовсім нещодавно вилізло зі свого огидного яйця. І хоч цю істоту вбити достатньо легко, не треба його недооцінювати — проживши всього тиждень-два, воно перетвориться щось набагато більше, страшніше та смертоносніше.
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Monsters/Spiderling.cfg:20
msgid "This huge spider is just a hatchling that has recently emerged from its disgusting egg. And although this creature is quite easy to kill, don't underestimate it - after living for just a week or two, it will turn into something much bigger, scarier and deadlier."
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=blade
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Monsters/Spiderling.cfg:25
msgid "fangs"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Braveheart, race=human
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Others/Braveheart.cfg:6
msgid "Braveheart"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Braveheart, race=human
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Others/Braveheart.cfg:41
msgid "The most skillful warriors of the Highlanders are called Bravehearts. They got their name for a reason: armed with impressive claymores, these warriors fearlessly rush into battle, cutting their enemies to pieces. Many legends about the deeds of the Bravehearts are told among the people of the Green Isle. Every king is proud to have such warriors under his banner."
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=blade
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Others/Braveheart.cfg:47
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Others/Braveheart.cfg:57
msgid "greatsword"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Brazier, race=mechanical
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Others/Brazier.cfg:4
msgid "Brazier"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Brazier, race=mechanical
#. Цей магічний світильник, що осяює все навколо себе утіленням самого Світла, було на якийсь час закликано до цього світу буквально з нічого потужною магією Даеоли. Хоч це й магічна істота, вона є повністю матеріальною, тому вона здатна як і завдавати шкоди ворогам, так і отримувати її у відповідь. 
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Others/Brazier.cfg:15
msgid "This magical brazier, which illuminates everything around it with the embodiment of Light itself, was summoned to this world for a time by the powerful magic of Daeola. Although it is a magical being, it is completely material, so it is capable of both inflicting harm on its enemies and receiving it in return."
msgstr ""

#. [scorch]: id=scorch
#. [attack]: type=arcane
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Others/Brazier.cfg:21
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Others/Brazier.cfg:31
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Others/Brazier.cfg:42
msgid "scorch"
msgstr ""

#. [scorch]: id=scorch
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Others/Brazier.cfg:22
msgid "At the start of this unit's turn, it deals 10 arcane damage to all adjacent enemy units."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Caravan, race=mechanical
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Others/Caravan.cfg:4
msgid "Caravan"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Caravan, race=mechanical
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Others/Caravan.cfg:17
msgid "Caravans are used to carry gold or supplies long distances. Because of the immense weight of the cargo this caravan carries, it is not nimble, but the driver can still try to drive off attackers with his whip."
msgstr ""

#. [special_note]
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Others/Caravan.cfg:19
msgid "The length of this unit’s improvised weapon allows it to strike first in defensive melee, but it cannot use it to attack."
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=impact
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Others/Caravan.cfg:25
msgid "whip"
msgstr ""

#. [firststrike]: id=deterrentstrike
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Others/Caravan.cfg:34
msgid "deterrent strike"
msgstr ""

#. [firststrike]: id=deterrentstrike
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Others/Caravan.cfg:35
msgid "This unit always strikes first with this attack if they are defending, but cannot attack with it at all."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=House_Cat, race=cats, gender=male
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Others/Cat.cfg:4
msgid "House Cat"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=House_Cat, race=cats, gender=male
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Others/Cat.cfg:13
msgid "An ordinary house cat, what else did you expect to read here?"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Crossbowman, race=human, gender=male
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Others/Crossbowman.cfg:5
msgid "Crossbowman"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Crossbowman, race=human, gender=male
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Others/Crossbowman.cfg:22
msgid "Some Bowman decide to take crossbows and axes to battle for more focus on their melee."
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=blade
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Others/Crossbowman.cfg:28
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Wesfolk/Warrior.cfg:23
msgid "axe"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Fisherman, race=human
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Others/Fisherman.cfg:4
msgid "Fisherman"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Gate Unit
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Others/Gate.cfg:4
msgid "Rusty Gate"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Gate Unit
#. Це просто чергові іржаві ворота з грубо обробленого заліза, що були створені сільським чи міським ковалем, в залежності від того де вони вам зустрілися.
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Others/Gate.cfg:14
msgid "This is just another rusty gate made of roughly worked iron, created by a village or city blacksmith, depending on where you found it."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Highlander, race=human
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Others/Highlander.cfg:6
msgid "Highlander"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Highlander, race=human
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Others/Highlander.cfg:40
msgid "In the mountains of the Green Isle live the mysterious tribes of the Highlanders. They are an ancient people who pride themselves on their warrior traditions and blacksmithing. There are rumors that the Highlanders are distant relatives of the Wesfolk, but no one knows for sure. Some kingdoms of the Green Isle have managed to make the Highlanders their vassals. In the event of war, Highlander units join their suzerain's army. They're far more dangerous than than a simple militia, especially in mountainous terrain."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Jeweler, race=human
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Others/Jeweler.cfg:4
msgid "Jeweler"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Nobleman, race=human
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Others/Nobleman.cfg:4
msgid "Nobleman"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Old Soldier, race=human
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Others/Old_Soldier.cfg:4
msgid "Old Soldier"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Old Soldier, race=human
#. Будь-який воїн, яким би сильним і вмілим він не був, не захищений від старості — якщо він не загинув у безлічі битв проти бандитів та солдатів ворожих королівств, рано чи пізно поважний вік наздожене його, перетворивши минулу міць та велич у крайню неміч та безпорадність.
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Others/Old_Soldier.cfg:13
msgid "Any warrior, no matter how strong and skilled, is not immune to old age - unless they have died in many battles against bandits and soldiers of enemy kingdoms, sooner or later seniority will overtake him or her, turning past power and greatness into extreme weakness and helplessness."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Statue Unit, race=mechanical
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Others/Statue.cfg:4
msgid "Statue"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Statue Unit, race=mechanical
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Others/Statue.cfg:24
msgid "A life-sized statue made of heavy granite from the nearby Scarhane's mine. This one is carved in the likeness of Gworwan XXI, one of the greatest kings of Blackmore, who ended a series of wars against the Kingdom of Woodlandor, seizing their territories on this side of Elderflow River."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Thug_Peasant
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Others/Villagers.cfg:15
msgid "Villager"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Thug_Peasant
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Others/Villagers.cfg:17
msgid "Peasants live in the small hamlets and villages scattered across the Green Isle countryside."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Bandit_Peasant
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Others/Villagers.cfg:25
msgid "Brawler"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Bandit_Peasant
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Others/Villagers.cfg:27
msgid "Not all disputes are settled by words alone. Some villagers, exceptionally strong and fiercely protective, rise to defend their homes and kin with their maces. They are part of their community's militia, ready to face any threat head-on."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Highwayman_Peasant
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Others/Villagers.cfg:35
msgid "Defender"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Highwayman_Peasant
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Others/Villagers.cfg:36
msgid "Having proven their mettle in countless skirmishes, the Village Defenders stand as an unwavering bulwark for their people. Their wisdom now extends beyond the local gossip to a profound understanding of defense tactics and community protection."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Ruffian_Peasant
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Others/Villagers.cfg:46
msgid "Youngster"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Footpad_Peasant
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Others/Villagers.cfg:56
msgid "Runner"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Footpad_Peasant
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Others/Villagers.cfg:58
msgid "These agile youths from the countryside may lack the might of seasoned warriors, but they make up for it with their speed and quick wits. They are often employed as couriers, swiftly delivering messages and supplies between settlements."
msgstr ""

#. [female]
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Others/Villagers.cfg:60
msgid "female^Peasant Youth"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Outlaw_Peasant
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Others/Villagers.cfg:69
msgid "Watchman"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Outlaw_Peasant
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Others/Villagers.cfg:71
msgid "The watchmen are men and women who protect the villages from marauders, both human and otherwise, that prowl the Green Isle countryside at night."
msgstr ""

#. [female]
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Others/Villagers.cfg:73
msgid "female^Watchwoman"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Fugitive_Peasant
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Others/Villagers.cfg:82
msgid "Borderer"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Fugitive_Peasant
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Others/Villagers.cfg:83
msgid "Border villages maintain militias dedicated to fending off hostiles. While these borderers are not trained and armed to up to military standards, their native toughness and knowledge of local conditions make them formidable on their home ground."
msgstr ""

#. [female]
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Others/Villagers.cfg:85
msgid "female^Borderer"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Poacher_Peasant
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Others/Villagers.cfg:107
msgid "Hunter"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Poacher_Peasant
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Others/Villagers.cfg:109
msgid "Villages, especially in wilder areas near frontiers, rely on hunters to bring in much of their food supply. Their stealth and intimate knowledge of local terrain can be valuable assets in combat."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Trapper_Peasant
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Others/Villagers.cfg:118
msgid "Trappers are skilled hunters who supply food and furs for several villages. Their hunting experience makes them most valuable at night and in forests and swamps."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Huntsman_Peasant
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Others/Villagers.cfg:126
msgid "Huntsmen have spent their lives in the backwoods and swamps of their wilderness homes. They can bullseye ferocious swamp rats and track anything that moves in their territory."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Web Unit
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Others/Web.cfg:4
msgid "Spider Web"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Web Unit
#. Скупчення павутиння небувалих розмірів, які зустрічаються глибоко під землею, куди не полізне жодна розумна людина. Цікаво, наскільки величезною є тварюка, що його створила?
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Others/Web.cfg:14
msgid "A cluster of spider webs of unprecedented size, found deep underground, where no sane person would venture. One wonders how huge the beast must be to have created it."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Dark Shade, race=undead
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Spirits/Dark_Shade.cfg:4
msgid "Dark Shade"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Dark Shade, race=undead
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Spirits/Dark_Shade.cfg:17
msgid "Dark shade is a spirit of something so dark that it was not allowed to exist in the real world. Only its shadow appears on walls and attacks the shadows of its victims - and the victims will get hurt too."
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=blade
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Spirits/Dark_Shade.cfg:73
msgid "claws"
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=arcane
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Spirits/Dark_Shade.cfg:85
msgid "soul sip"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Elemental Air, race=monster, description=
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Spirits/Elemental_Air.cfg:4
msgid "Air Elemental"
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=impact
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Spirits/Elemental_Air.cfg:64
msgid "hurricane"
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=arcane
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Spirits/Elemental_Air.cfg:76
msgid "small lightning"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Elemental Fire, race=monster, description=
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Spirits/Elemental_Fire.cfg:4
msgid "Fire Elemental"
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=fire
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Spirits/Elemental_Fire.cfg:71
msgid "burning fist"
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=fire
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Spirits/Elemental_Fire.cfg:83
msgid "spark"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Elemental Rock, race=monster
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Spirits/Elemental_Rock.cfg:4
msgid "Rock Elemental"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Elemental Rock, race=monster
#. Зазвичай місця, що випромінують магію, є домівкою для різноманітних духів природи, що з невідомих причин виявляють себе фізичною формою, захищаючи своє улюблене місце від тих, хто посміє потурбувати їхній спокій. Проте в випадку з цим Rock Elementals не все так однозначно — кам'яні ісполини мають на собі дивні намальовані знаки, що явно натякають на їхнє штучне походження, проте правди ніхто ніколи вже не дізнається...
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Spirits/Elemental_Rock.cfg:19
msgid "Usually, places that radiate magic are home to various spirits of nature that, for unknown reasons, manifest themselves in physical form, protecting their favorite site from those who dare to disturb their peace. However, in the case of these Rock Elementals, everything is not so clear - living stones have strange symbols on their bodies that clearly hint at their artificial origin, but no one will ever know the truth..."
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=impact
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Spirits/Elemental_Rock.cfg:70
msgid "hit"
msgstr ""

